  "finding_info": {
    "uid": "f653f8ada817ab7b758163f8007e32f5",
    "title": "Agent account decoded encoded data",
    "desc": "A non-human service or agent account ran a decoder - base64 -d, base32 -d, xxd -r, uudecode, or openssl with a decode flag. Decoding encoded bytes is how an obfuscated payload is unpacked before it runs (MITRE T1140): an attacker who has driven the agent off its task, or a prompt injection, stages the next stage as base64/hex so it slips past a reviewer reading the session. On a human login decoding is routine; by the agent it is off-pattern, so the rule is scoped by account name - it is the *who* that makes it signal. deobfuscate_and_run catches a decode piped straight into a shell host-wide (a stronger, everyone signal); this catches the agent decoding at all.\nThis is an \"agentic AI detection\" rule: a detection written for the behaviour of an autonomous agent, a class SigmaHQ does not yet cover. See rules/agent/README.md.",
